A stack is a linear data structure that follows the Last-In-First-Out (LIFO) principle. It can be implemented using a linked list, where each element of the stack is represented as a node. The head of the linked list acts as the top of the stack.Declaration of Stack using Linked ListA stack can be implemented using a linked list where we maintain:A Node structure/class that contains:data → to store the element.next → pointer/reference to the next node in the stack.A pointer/reference top that always points to the current top node of the stack.Initially, top = null to represent an empty stack.Try It Yourself
